From a9c99e4b48e7749dad287ecb892fb14348012c66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: phlink <dev@phlink.local>
Date: Thu, 30 Apr 2026 00:50:28 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] phlink: phase 10.05 Windows update helper

Adds win-only phlink_update_helper.exe and apply logic:

  phlink_update_helper --apply <staging_dir> <target_exe>
                                <expected_signer_cn>

Pipeline:
  1. Read staged.json.
  2. Confirm payload exists.
  3. WinVerifyTrust (WINTRUST_ACTION_GENERIC_VERIFY_V2,
     WTD_REVOKE_WHOLECHAIN) Authenticode validation.
  4. CryptQueryObject + CryptMsgGetParam to extract the signer
     certificate; CertGetNameStringW(CERT_NAME_SIMPLE_DISPLAY_TYPE)
     to obtain its subject CN; pin against the expected EV-cert
     subject.
  5. MoveFileExW(MOVEFILE_REPLACE_EXISTING |
     MOVEFILE_DELAY_UNTIL_REBOOT) to swap the running phlink.exe
     at next reboot.
  6. Delete staged.json.

Tests cover argument validation and missing-staged.json. Authenticode
+ subject-pin paths require a real EV-signed exe and are deferred
to CI on the windows nightly build (10-08).

Build target gated on is_win; mac compiles only the GN graph (gn
gen succeeds; ninja no-op on mac since the win subgraph is unreferenced
by non-platform-gated GN).

Refs phlink phase 10-05.
